        <mxCell id="oTV51KeiLnIpI_8r1Urz-37" value="&lt;font size=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;What was the historical context throughout the chain of custodianship?&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=#666666;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#D5D5D5;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;gradientColor=none;" parent="oTV51KeiLnIpI_8r1Urz-36" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry width="180" height="170" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle width="180" height="170" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="oTV51KeiLnIpI_8r1Urz-38" value="&lt;font size=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Three significant time periods: the crucifixion of Jesus, the destruction of the Jerusalem Temple, and the Bar Kokhba revolt&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 2px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;From Jesus&#39; ministry (30–33 AD) until the destruction of the Temple in 70 AD, the earliest Christian community existed as a small, multilingual&amp;nbsp;&lt;span&gt;Jewish&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;sect within the Roman Empire. Oral reports about Jesus circulated both publicly and privately and were centered around the Church of Jerusalem.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 2px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;After 70 AD, Christianity spread more rapidly across the Roman Empire, shifting from a primarily Jewish and Aramaic context to a predominantly Gentile and Greek-speaking one - even while facing persecution. Written accounts multiplied and circulated during this phase, including traditions that were later deemed heretical.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 2px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;After the failed Bar Kokhba revolt (132–136 AD), the split between Christianity and Rabbinic Judaism became permanent. Christianity developed a more formal institutional structure, and Church Fathers began defending and consolidating apostolic tradition against rival claims. After Constantine&#39;s conversion in 312 AD, Rome emerged as the new capital of Christianity.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=inherit;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#CCFFCC;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;strokeWidth=1;verticalAlign=top;fontColor=#000000;spacing=2;spacingLeft=1;spacingRight=1;spacingBottom=0;spacingTop=-2;" parent="oTV51KeiLnIpI_8r1Urz-36" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="180" width="315" height="170" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle width="315" height="170" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="oTV51KeiLnIpI_8r1Urz-39" value="&lt;font size=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Three significant time periods: the time of Quranic revelation, the time of Quranic textual standardization, and the time of Hadith compilation&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 2px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;The Quran was revealed to Prophet Muhammad over 23 years (610-632 AD, 13 in Makkah and 10 in Madinah) uniting warring, independent tribes into a single nation and extending its message into northern Africa and southern Europe.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 2px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;After the Prophet&#39;s death in 632 AD, the next 4 caliphs standardized the Quranic text to combat the threat of memorizers falling in battle, as well to ensure its meaning would be consistent among the Arab tribes with different dialects.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 2px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;After Uthman standardized the Quranic dialect (between 560-656 AD), Islam expanded beyond Arabia, making it harder to verify which reports about the Prophet were authentic.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;From 684-915 AD, hadith compilations were written and a formal science of authentication emerged. This period also marked the beginning of the Islamic Golden Age, during which many branches of knowledge - including, but not limited to, Hadith - were developed and systematized.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=inherit;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#CCE5FF;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;verticalAlign=top;fontColor=#000000;spacing=2;spacingLeft=1;spacingRight=1;spacingBottom=0;spacingTop=-2;" parent="oTV51KeiLnIpI_8r1Urz-36" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="495" width="315" height="170" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle width="315" height="170" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="oTV51KeiLnIpI_8r1Urz-40" style="shape=tableRow;horizontal=0;startSize=0;swimlaneHead=0;swimlaneBody=0;strokeColor=inherit;top=0;left=0;bottom=0;right=0;collapsible=0;dropTarget=0;fillColor=none;points=[[0,0.5],[1,0.5]];portConstraint=eastwest;fontSize=16;" parent="oTV51KeiLnIpI_8r1Urz-35" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="170" width="810" height="185" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="oTV51KeiLnIpI_8r1Urz-41" value="&lt;font size=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;What were the standards of testimony and custodianship in this time?&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=#666666;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#D5D5D5;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;gradientColor=none;" parent="oTV51KeiLnIpI_8r1Urz-40" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry width="180" height="185" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle width="180" height="185" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="oTV51KeiLnIpI_8r1Urz-42" value="&lt;font size=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Eyewitness testimony, gradually shifting towards scholarly textual standardization&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 2px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;In the 1st-century Jewish context, valid testimony required at least two credible witnesses (free, adult males without conflict of interest), based on Deuteronomy 19:15 and Mishnaic traditions. Roman standards similarly valued reputable eyewitnesses (non-criminals) and oral testimony in court, with writing reserved for limited formal records.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 2px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;After 70 AD, as Christianity spread under Roman persecution, standards shifted toward Greco-Roman historiography and Jewish diaspora oral practices, resulting in semi-verbatim preservation and the growth of written accounts that defended core narratives against competing versions. From the 2nd-4th centuries, Roman legal writing expanded, while Christian custodianship formalized around three criteria: apostolic origin, catholicity (universal acceptance), and non-contradiction with established faith.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 2px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;Thus, the Bible&#39;s guiding standard was credible eyewitness testimony with faithful transmission of meaning and message, not verbatim memorization. This is reflected in the numerous early textual variants, which arose from scribes attempting to better preserve and transmit the intended truth than the original.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=inherit;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#CCFFCC;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;strokeWidth=1;verticalAlign=top;fontColor=#000000;spacing=2;spacingLeft=1;spacingRight=1;spacingBottom=0;spacingTop=-2;" parent="oTV51KeiLnIpI_8r1Urz-40" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="180" width="315" height="185" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle width="315" height="185" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="oTV51KeiLnIpI_8r1Urz-43" value="&lt;font size=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Communally verbatim oral transmission&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 2px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237)); font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;Pre-Islamic Arabia was a predominantly oral culture that lacked literary and textual presence. As a result, they preserved history through memory, oral performance, and poetic competition rather than writing - which was a&amp;nbsp;skill that was seen as&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237)); font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;a source of immense cultural pride and honor.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237)); font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;Eloquence, genealogy, and precise memorization were central to cultural identity, and written materials - though scarce - were secondary aids to the superior discipline of trained memory.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 2px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;This same system continued during the Quran&#39;s revelation and after, producing mass, communal, verbatim memorization, later mirrored in Hadith sciences as well. Daily prayers, being communal and audible, required Quranic recitation - meaning any mistake could be corrected publicly, reinforcing collective preservation. As a result, the oral Quran functioned as a primary, living authority, while also anchoring its textual standardization and safeguarding its exact wording.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=inherit;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#CCE5FF;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;verticalAlign=top;fontColor=#000000;spacing=2;spacingLeft=1;spacingRight=1;spacingBottom=0;spacingTop=-2;" parent="oTV51KeiLnIpI_8r1Urz-40" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="495" width="315" height="185" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle width="315" height="185" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="oTV51KeiLnIpI_8r1Urz-44" style="shape=tableRow;horizontal=0;startSize=0;swimlaneHead=0;swimlaneBody=0;strokeColor=inherit;top=0;left=0;bottom=0;right=0;collapsible=0;dropTarget=0;fillColor=none;points=[[0,0.5],[1,0.5]];portConstraint=eastwest;fontSize=16;" parent="oTV51KeiLnIpI_8r1Urz-35" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="355" width="810" height="295" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="oTV51KeiLnIpI_8r1Urz-45" value="&lt;font size=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Is there anything anachronistic (historically or logically out of place) about the claim or its custodianship?&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=#666666;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#D5D5D5;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;gradientColor=none;" parent="oTV51KeiLnIpI_8r1Urz-44" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry width="180" height="295" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle width="180" height="295" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="oTV51KeiLnIpI_8r1Urz-46" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;font size=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Many examples against Jewish expectations&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 2px; text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Social and Cultural&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;-&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; text-align: center; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;Female testimony was not considered credible, yet all 4 Gospels report that the first witnesses of Jesus&#39; resurrection were women.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px; background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237));&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;-&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; text-align: center; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;Jews and Samaritans were hostile toward one another, yet Jesus is depicted engaging a Samaritan positively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px; background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237));&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;-&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; text-align: center; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;Despite purity laws and social boundaries, Jesus is shown dining with, healing, and ministering to those considered &quot;unclean&quot;, including tax collectors, lepers, prostitutes, and other outcasts.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px; background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237));&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;-&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; text-align: center; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;In a culture where superiors would not submit to inferiors, Jesus is baptized by John in an act of symbolic cleansing - despite John being lower in status.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237)); font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 2px; text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Theological&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px; background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237));&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;-&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; text-align: center; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;Although Jewish monotheism rejected the idea that God could be a man, Jesus is depicted as divine - God Himself. However, relative to Greco-Roman beliefs, this claim would not have seemed anachronistic.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px; background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237));&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;-&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; text-align: center; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;Although Jewish tradition emphasized God&#39;s open and jealous self-disclosure, Jesus&#39; divine identity is portrayed as implied or veiled rather than explicit.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Although the expected Messiah would triumph, Jesus is portrayed as crucified by Rome - a shameful death reserved for criminals. The resurrection resolves this issue, but the very concept of a dying-rising figure was not unusual in Greco-Roman contexts.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Despite the expectation that authentic messages would be clear and consistent from the start (and orally transmitted as such), the Gospels appear to reflect a rising Christology, with Jesus&#39;s divinity becoming more easily identifiable in later-written texts.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 2px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;Notes: Jesus also reinterpreted Jewish understanding of the law (such as being more lenient with stoning, yet more strict with divorce), but these are non-fundamental. Also, regarding the rising Christology: some argue that this sign of changing what Jesus himself claimed, while others defend by defining it as progressive revelation, where different authors highlight different aspects of the complete, unified truth.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=inherit;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#CCFFCC;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;strokeWidth=1;verticalAlign=top;fontColor=#000000;spacing=2;spacingLeft=1;spacingRight=1;spacingBottom=0;spacingTop=-2;" parent="oTV51KeiLnIpI_8r1Urz-44" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="180" width="315" height="295" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle width="315" height="295" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="oTV51KeiLnIpI_8r1Urz-47" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot; size=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Many examples against the 7th century Arabian context&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 2px; text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;Social and Cultural&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Females were seen as inferior to males, yet the Quran states that men and women are equal under the sight of God&lt;/font&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;. When women weren&#39;t able to own property, inherit wealth, and consent to marriage, now they can. Where daughters could be buried alive due to her birth dishonoring her family, now that was considered a crime.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;font&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Despite deeply embedded tribalism (where &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;an individual&#39;s identity, protection, nobility, and honor were entirely dependent on their tribe)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;font&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;, the Quran states that the most noble in the sight of God are those who are most righteous.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Despite Arabian expertise and history of established poetry and eloquence, the Quran&#39;s structure does not fall in any prior literary or oral genres.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;-&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; text-align: center; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;Despite the Quran being considered the height of eloquence (even by its opponents), it is attributed to Muhammad - a man known to be illiterate. Yet there are many instances where the verses are immediately revealed in response to live, unpredictable situations - without later revision, proofreading, correction, or alteration to the original words.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 2px; text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;Theological&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- In a context in which religious scriptures are written by men (and are defended as divinely guided), the Quran claims to be authored by God Himself and&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;He will be the one to preserve it.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 8px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Despite being geographically surrounded by polytheists (denying the hereafter), Jews (rejecting an Arab prophet), and Christians (upholding Trinitarian or heterodox views), the Quran proclaims a pure monotheism distinct from all three - though closest in form to Jewish belief.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 2px; background-color: transparent; text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;Notes: the Quran also reinterpreted Jewish understanding of the law (such as explaining why the laws were so strict) and Jesus&#39; identity as pure human being, but these are non-fundamental. Also, s&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;ome argue that the Quran&#39;s historical and natural claims are uniquely and strikingly consistent with established history and science, but&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;that is also non-fundamental.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=inherit;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#CCE5FF;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;verticalAlign=top;fontColor=#000000;spacing=2;spacingLeft=1;spacingRight=1;spacingBottom=0;spacingTop=-2;" parent="oTV51KeiLnIpI_8r1Urz-44" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="495" width="315" height="295" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle width="315" height="295" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <UserObject label="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font&gt;4. Alignment with Historical Context&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;" link="data:page/id,vzxsm3Ze7Mdvi2NmskRt" id="oTV51KeiLnIpI_8r1Urz-48">
          <mxCell style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=18;fillColor=#D5E8D4;gradientColor=#97D077;strokeColor=#82B366;" parent="i9uRf7bMxYR_9wg2oDwC-0" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry width="810.0000000000001" height="44.9999999999999" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="" link="data:page/id,Z-l9n-z4b5n7cfZyjVss" id="Otdqm500R71XWhVRFQ-1-0">
          <mxCell style="group" parent="oTV51KeiLnIpI_8r1Urz-1" vertex="1" connectable="0">
            <mxGeometry x="780" y="2220" width="50" height="50" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="Otdqm500R71XWhVRFQ-1-1" value="" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;pointerEvents=0;align=center;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;fillColor=#E6E6E6;gradientColor=none;strokeColor=none;rotation=-180;opacity=1;" parent="Otdqm500R71XWhVRFQ-1-0" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="3.552713678800501e-15" width="50" height="50" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
