        <mxCell id="j6Lz0SjBER47GQh4H0wA-5" parent="Oy0AfYZwk4wytR56GQPK-1" style="shape=table;startSize=0;container=1;collapsible=0;childLayout=tableLayout;fontSize=1;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="145" width="810" y="35" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="j6Lz0SjBER47GQh4H0wA-6" parent="j6Lz0SjBER47GQh4H0wA-5" style="shape=tableRow;horizontal=0;startSize=0;swimlaneHead=0;swimlaneBody=0;strokeColor=inherit;top=0;left=0;bottom=0;right=0;collapsible=0;dropTarget=0;fillColor=none;points=[[0,0.5],[1,0.5]];portConstraint=eastwest;fontSize=16;swimlaneFillColor=none;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="145" width="810" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="j6Lz0SjBER47GQh4H0wA-8" parent="j6Lz0SjBER47GQh4H0wA-6" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=inherit;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#CCFFCC;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;strokeWidth=1;verticalAlign=middle;fontColor=#000000;spacing=2;spacingLeft=1;spacingRight=1;spacingBottom=0;spacingTop=-2;swimlaneFillColor=none;gradientColor=#CCE5FF;gradientDirection=east;align=center;" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 9px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Christianity looks more like a corrupted version of Islam, while Islam looks more like a corrected version of Christianity&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 2px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;Both religions affirm that God is One, ultimately loving, perfectly just and merciful, that He values and merits righteousness, and that He alone permits everything - including both our own wills and Satan’s influence. However, they manifest these same truths in very different ways, leading to fundamentally significant differences. As a result, this question does not deny the existence of any of these attributes on either side, but rather explores the nuances in how they manifest - allowing us to identify which drift (from one to the other) more closely matches with how a deceiver would act (assuming one side is fully True).&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 2px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;If we assume Christianity is the original truth, then Islam&#39;s differences look like a drift that &lt;i&gt;sharpens&lt;/i&gt; God&#39;s oneness and rationality, &lt;i&gt;magnifies&lt;/i&gt; mercy and accountability, and &lt;i&gt;diminishes&lt;/i&gt; the emphasis on Satan&#39;s power. Likewise, if we assume Islam is the original truth, then Christianity&#39;s differences look like a drift that &lt;i&gt;increases&lt;/i&gt; God&#39;s expectations, &lt;i&gt;emphasizes&lt;/i&gt; Satan&#39;s power, &lt;i&gt;reduces&lt;/i&gt; God&#39;s oneness and original mercy, and &lt;i&gt;diminishes&lt;/i&gt; the salvific function of our good deeds, our spiritual status, and rationality. Neither one sacrifices God&#39;s justice, grace, and the reality of the law - merely redirecting how they manifest, as they are entirely coherent (within their own narratives).&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 2px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;From this comparison, it is clear that a deceiver would align more with corrupting Islam into Christianity. In line with previous sections&#39; conclusions, Islam presents a more consistent divine system: God&#39;s transcendence is greater (without sacrificing intimate closeness), rationality is sharper (without denying mystery or our limits), God&#39;s mercy is immediate (as Christianity delays the application of Jesus&#39; atonement with Adam&#39;s sin), and righteousness and repentance are valued over sin (without removing our accountability or sin&#39;s ability to condemn). Even our status is more honored in Islam, with Adam being forgiven from his sin and us being born pure (rather than being punished and entering into a fallen state - &lt;i&gt;like Satan did in both narratives&lt;/i&gt;).&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 2px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;So, if a deceiver wants to misguide from the truth as much as possible, then reducing God&#39;s transcendence, mercy, and rationality, lowering our status, elevating Satan&#39;s emphasis, and redirecting our faith and hope in a way that God did not authorize all align with the transition from Islam to Christianity (making Islam look like Christianity&#39;s correction).&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="145" width="810" as="geometry">
