        <mxCell id="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-2" parent="j8RR2Dj3IIjpAT4dpo4w-2" style="shape=table;startSize=0;container=1;collapsible=0;childLayout=tableLayout;fontSize=1;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="535" width="789.9999999999999" y="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-3" parent="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-2" style="shape=tableRow;horizontal=0;startSize=0;swimlaneHead=0;swimlaneBody=0;strokeColor=inherit;top=0;left=0;bottom=0;right=0;collapsible=0;dropTarget=0;fillColor=none;points=[[0,0.5],[1,0.5]];portConstraint=eastwest;fontSize=16;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="85" width="789.9999999999999" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-4" parent="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-3" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=#666666;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#F8CECC;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=2;spacingLeft=1;spacingRight=1;spacingBottom=0;spacingTop=-2;gradientColor=#EA6B66;align=center;strokeWidth=0;" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;&quot;&gt;1. Pursuit of Truth&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="85" width="115" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle height="85" width="115" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-5" parent="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-3" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=#666666;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#DFDFDF;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;verticalAlign=top;spacing=2;spacingLeft=1;spacingRight=1;spacingBottom=0;spacingTop=-2;gradientColor=none;align=left;strokeWidth=0;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- You are saying that truth is not defined externally: &quot;reality&quot; is [fundamentally] subjective and not something you have to submit to, nor can anyone else decide what your &quot;truth&quot; is.&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="85" width="225" x="115" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle height="85" width="225" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-10" parent="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-3" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=#666666;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#DFDFDF;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;verticalAlign=top;spacing=2;spacingLeft=1;spacingRight=1;spacingBottom=0;spacingTop=-2;gradientColor=none;align=left;strokeWidth=0;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- If the truth is not decided externally, then it must be decided internally - meaning that conflicting beliefs are equally &quot;true&quot; for different people.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 2px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- You can no longer say other beliefs are &quot;wrong&quot; (except that you &quot;don&#39;t like it&quot;): they are simply living their truth, just like you.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="85" width="225" x="340" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle height="85" width="225" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-11" parent="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-3" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=#666666;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#DFDFDF;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;verticalAlign=top;spacing=2;spacingLeft=1;spacingRight=1;spacingBottom=0;spacingTop=-2;gradientColor=none;align=left;strokeWidth=0;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- You no longer distinguish truth from falsehood; you only distinguish what you affirm from what you reject.&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="85" width="225" x="565" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle height="85" width="225" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-12" parent="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-2" style="shape=tableRow;horizontal=0;startSize=0;swimlaneHead=0;swimlaneBody=0;strokeColor=inherit;top=0;left=0;bottom=0;right=0;collapsible=0;dropTarget=0;fillColor=none;points=[[0,0.5],[1,0.5]];portConstraint=eastwest;fontSize=16;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="55" width="789.9999999999999" y="85" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-13" parent="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-12" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=#666666;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#FFDEC9;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=2;spacingLeft=1;spacingRight=1;spacingBottom=0;spacingTop=-2;gradientColor=#FFB663;align=center;strokeWidth=0;" value="&lt;b style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;2. Discovering Reality&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="55" width="115" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle height="55" width="115" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-14" parent="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-12" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=#666666;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#DFDFDF;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;verticalAlign=top;spacing=2;spacingLeft=1;spacingRight=1;spacingBottom=0;spacingTop=-2;gradientColor=none;align=left;strokeWidth=0;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- You are separating truth (or its accessibility) from reality and awareness.&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="55" width="225" x="115" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle height="55" width="225" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-15" parent="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-12" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=#666666;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#DFDFDF;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;verticalAlign=top;spacing=2;spacingLeft=1;spacingRight=1;spacingBottom=0;spacingTop=-2;gradientColor=none;align=left;strokeWidth=0;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Either:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;a. speculation can count as truth&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;b. truth is unattainable in principle&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="55" width="225" x="340" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle height="55" width="225" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-16" parent="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-12" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=#666666;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#DFDFDF;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;verticalAlign=top;spacing=2;spacingLeft=1;spacingRight=1;spacingBottom=0;spacingTop=-2;gradientColor=none;align=left;strokeWidth=0;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- If either occurs, then a liar has the same [epistemic] authority as a truthful person: both appeal to unverifiable information, and all claims become equally undefeated.&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="55" width="225" x="565" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle height="55" width="225" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-17" parent="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-2" style="shape=tableRow;horizontal=0;startSize=0;swimlaneHead=0;swimlaneBody=0;strokeColor=inherit;top=0;left=0;bottom=0;right=0;collapsible=0;dropTarget=0;fillColor=none;points=[[0,0.5],[1,0.5]];portConstraint=eastwest;fontSize=16;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="60" width="789.9999999999999" y="140" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-18" parent="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-17" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=#666666;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#FFF2CC;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=2;spacingLeft=1;spacingRight=1;spacingBottom=0;spacingTop=-2;gradientColor=#FFD966;align=center;strokeWidth=0;" value="&lt;b style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;3. Building Confidence&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="60" width="115" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle height="60" width="115" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-19" parent="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-17" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=#666666;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#DFDFDF;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;verticalAlign=top;spacing=2;spacingLeft=1;spacingRight=1;spacingBottom=0;spacingTop=-2;gradientColor=none;align=left;strokeWidth=0;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- You are equating assertion, sincerity, or strength of belief with justification and proof.&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="60" width="225" x="115" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle height="60" width="225" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-20" parent="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-17" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=#666666;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#DFDFDF;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;verticalAlign=top;spacing=2;spacingLeft=1;spacingRight=1;spacingBottom=0;spacingTop=-2;gradientColor=none;align=left;strokeWidth=0;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- You now must accept the validity of:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;a. circular/baseless justification&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;b. confidence built on ignorance and speculation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="60" width="225" x="340" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle height="60" width="225" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-21" parent="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-17" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=#666666;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#DFDFDF;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;verticalAlign=top;spacing=2;spacingLeft=1;spacingRight=1;spacingBottom=0;spacingTop=-2;gradientColor=none;align=left;strokeWidth=0;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Fabrication and lies become indistinguishable from truth, because fabricators and liars can build closed loops too.&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="60" width="225" x="565" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle height="60" width="225" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-22" parent="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-2" style="shape=tableRow;horizontal=0;startSize=0;swimlaneHead=0;swimlaneBody=0;strokeColor=inherit;top=0;left=0;bottom=0;right=0;collapsible=0;dropTarget=0;fillColor=none;points=[[0,0.5],[1,0.5]];portConstraint=eastwest;fontSize=16;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="70" width="789.9999999999999" y="200" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-23" parent="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-22" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=#666666;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#D5E8D4;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=2;spacingLeft=1;spacingRight=1;spacingBottom=0;spacingTop=-2;gradientColor=#97D077;align=center;strokeWidth=0;" value="&lt;b style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;4. Defining God&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="70" width="115" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle height="70" width="115" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-24" parent="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-22" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=#666666;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#DFDFDF;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;verticalAlign=top;spacing=2;spacingLeft=1;spacingRight=1;spacingBottom=0;spacingTop=-2;gradientColor=none;align=left;strokeWidth=0;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- You are separating the definition (ie. fundamental understanding) of God from correspondence with reality.&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="70" width="225" x="115" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle height="70" width="225" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-25" parent="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-22" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=#666666;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#DFDFDF;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;verticalAlign=top;spacing=2;spacingLeft=1;spacingRight=1;spacingBottom=0;spacingTop=-2;gradientColor=none;align=left;strokeWidth=0;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Theological contradictions can now be treated as mysteries, protecting any false belief from being identified as such.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 2px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Faith can now be separated from reason.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="70" width="225" x="340" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle height="70" width="225" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-26" parent="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-22" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=#666666;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#DFDFDF;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;verticalAlign=top;spacing=2;spacingLeft=1;spacingRight=1;spacingBottom=0;spacingTop=-2;gradientColor=none;align=left;strokeWidth=0;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- If mysteries are indistinguishable from contradictions, then no theological claim can ever be identified as false, for faith can now occur without (or against) reason - leaving deception without a mechanism for detection.&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="70" width="225" x="565" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle height="70" width="225" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-27" parent="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-2" style="shape=tableRow;horizontal=0;startSize=0;swimlaneHead=0;swimlaneBody=0;strokeColor=inherit;top=0;left=0;bottom=0;right=0;collapsible=0;dropTarget=0;fillColor=none;points=[[0,0.5],[1,0.5]];portConstraint=eastwest;fontSize=16;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="85" width="789.9999999999999" y="270" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-28" parent="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-27" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=#666666;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#DAE8FC;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=2;spacingLeft=1;spacingRight=1;spacingBottom=0;spacingTop=-2;gradientColor=#7EA6E0;align=center;strokeWidth=0;" value="&lt;b style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;5. Alignment with Reality&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="85" width="115" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle height="85" width="115" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-29" parent="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-27" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=#666666;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#DFDFDF;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;verticalAlign=top;spacing=2;spacingLeft=1;spacingRight=1;spacingBottom=0;spacingTop=-2;gradientColor=none;align=left;strokeWidth=0;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Either:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;a. you reject a previous inference&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;b. you&#39;ve inferred something not mentioned above that opposes the deduced conclusions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="85" width="225" x="115" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle height="85" width="225" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-30" parent="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-27" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=#666666;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#DFDFDF;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;verticalAlign=top;spacing=2;spacingLeft=1;spacingRight=1;spacingBottom=0;spacingTop=-2;gradientColor=none;align=left;strokeWidth=0;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Either:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;a. speculation can refute or prove claims&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;b. open, blind rejection of clear observation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;c. reality does not lead to metaphysics&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;d. you have knowledge not mentioned here&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="85" width="225" x="340" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle height="85" width="225" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-31" parent="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-27" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=#666666;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#DFDFDF;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;verticalAlign=top;spacing=2;spacingLeft=1;spacingRight=1;spacingBottom=0;spacingTop=-2;gradientColor=none;align=left;strokeWidth=0;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- If no additional [non-speculative] inference is found to oppose these conclusions, then both speculation and blind rejection can be used to justify both truth and falsehood.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 2px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Otherwise, valid inferences must be stated clearly and defended non-speculatively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="85" width="225" x="565" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle height="85" width="225" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-32" parent="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-2" style="shape=tableRow;horizontal=0;startSize=0;swimlaneHead=0;swimlaneBody=0;strokeColor=inherit;top=0;left=0;bottom=0;right=0;collapsible=0;dropTarget=0;fillColor=none;points=[[0,0.5],[1,0.5]];portConstraint=eastwest;fontSize=16;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="95" width="789.9999999999999" y="355" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-33" parent="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-32" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=#666666;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#DCDBFC;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=2;spacingLeft=1;spacingRight=1;spacingBottom=0;spacingTop=-2;gradientColor=#9393E0;align=center;strokeWidth=0;" value="&lt;b style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;6. Historical Comparison&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="95" width="115" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle height="95" width="115" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-34" parent="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-32" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=#666666;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#DFDFDF;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;verticalAlign=top;spacing=2;spacingLeft=1;spacingRight=1;spacingBottom=0;spacingTop=-2;gradientColor=none;align=left;strokeWidth=0;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Either:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;a. the evidence is wrong, or some is missing&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;b. you reject the process of building confidence in historical claims, specifically traceability and/or resistance to fabrication&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="95" width="225" x="115" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle height="95" width="225" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-35" parent="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-32" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=#666666;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#DFDFDF;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;verticalAlign=top;spacing=2;spacingLeft=1;spacingRight=1;spacingBottom=0;spacingTop=-2;gradientColor=none;align=left;strokeWidth=0;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- If evidence is wrong, then it requires proof, or a competing explanation that encompasses the same data - without appealing to speculation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 2px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Otherwise, you accept the validity of:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;a. trusting or rejecting unknown links, simply based on speculation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;b. circular/baseless authentication&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="95" width="225" x="340" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle height="95" width="225" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-36" parent="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-32" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=#666666;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#DFDFDF;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;verticalAlign=top;spacing=2;spacingLeft=1;spacingRight=1;spacingBottom=0;spacingTop=-2;gradientColor=none;align=left;strokeWidth=0;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- True revelation becomes indistinguishable from fabrication, as fabricated sources depend on trusting unknown links and accepting circular/&lt;br&gt;baseless authentication.&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="95" width="225" x="565" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle height="95" width="225" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-37" parent="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-2" style="shape=tableRow;horizontal=0;startSize=0;swimlaneHead=0;swimlaneBody=0;strokeColor=inherit;top=0;left=0;bottom=0;right=0;collapsible=0;dropTarget=0;fillColor=none;points=[[0,0.5],[1,0.5]];portConstraint=eastwest;fontSize=16;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="85" width="789.9999999999999" y="450" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-38" parent="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-37" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=#666666;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#E6D0DE;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=2;spacingLeft=1;spacingRight=1;spacingBottom=0;spacingTop=-2;gradientColor=#D5739D;align=center;strokeWidth=0;" value="&lt;b style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;7. Non-Fundamental Comparison&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="85" width="115" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle height="85" width="115" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-39" parent="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-37" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=#666666;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#DFDFDF;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;verticalAlign=top;spacing=2;spacingLeft=1;spacingRight=1;spacingBottom=0;spacingTop=-2;gradientColor=none;align=left;strokeWidth=0;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Either:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;a. the evidence is wrong, or some is missing&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;b. you reject the relevance or process of assessing theological coherence&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="85" width="225" x="115" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle height="85" width="225" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-40" parent="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-37" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=#666666;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#DFDFDF;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;verticalAlign=top;spacing=2;spacingLeft=1;spacingRight=1;spacingBottom=0;spacingTop=-2;gradientColor=none;align=left;strokeWidth=0;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- If evidence is wrong, then it requires proof.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 2px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Otherwise: you accept that comparative coherence doesn&#39;t apply to theology, as the results only appear that way due to your own, permanent ignorance - which can never be resolved.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="85" width="225" x="340" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle height="85" width="225" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-41" parent="tUv_EsOKeU8NKWYyWOEs-37" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=#666666;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#DFDFDF;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;verticalAlign=top;spacing=2;spacingLeft=1;spacingRight=1;spacingBottom=0;spacingTop=-2;gradientColor=none;align=left;strokeWidth=0;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Internal coherence is no longer required as a metric for a religion&#39;s truth - meaning that the internal claims of false religions are equally valid, for the falsehood is masked by ignorance of the fullness of the truth.&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="85" width="225" x="565" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle height="85" width="225" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram name="Results &amp; Conclusion (3/3)" id="zjUQ_zZ1L1Msfoq7Qf02">
    <mxGraphModel dx="961" dy="-9035" grid="1" gridSize="5" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="850" pageHeight="1100" background="#CCCCCC" math="0" shadow="0" adaptiveColors="none">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="3-4-euxaZI7sU592ncQ1-0" />
        <mxCell id="3-4-euxaZI7sU592ncQ1-1" parent="3-4-euxaZI7sU592ncQ1-0" />
        <UserObject label="Results and Conclusion (3/3&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;" link="data:page/id,lkuSvPZcJC7dHRsydWrw" id="3-4-euxaZI7sU592ncQ1-2">
          <mxCell parent="3-4-euxaZI7sU592ncQ1-1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#E6E6E6;fontSize=20;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="50" width="810" x="20" y="9920" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="3-4-euxaZI7sU592ncQ1-41" parent="3-4-euxaZI7sU592ncQ1-1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;pointerEvents=0;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;gradientColor=#b3b3b3;strokeColor=#666666;spacingTop=6;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;movable=1;resizable=1;rotatable=1;deletable=1;editable=1;locked=0;connectable=1;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Conclusion&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 4px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;This project is not designed to present a personal &quot;preference&quot; among competing worldviews, but to demystify the whole subject and make navigating between them properly accessible to anyone interested in pursuing the Truth. The central insight is simple: &lt;b&gt;if you want to distinguish truth from falsehood, then you must reject any approach that makes falsehood indistinguishable from truth.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;This is why each step of the sieve matters: each step removes one more way of &quot;getting to an answer&quot; that can be used equally well by truth and falsehood, while doing so in a hierarchical way that narrows down the possibilities in an efficient, practical, and easy to understand way - effectively forbidding entire families of answers:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- It forbids &quot;truth by preference/affirmation&quot;, because preference can affirm falsehood - allowing&amp;nbsp;&lt;i&gt;any&lt;/i&gt;&amp;nbsp;comforting worldview to be &quot;true&quot;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- It forbids &quot;truth by speculation&quot;, because unverifiable possibilities can always be invented - allowing&amp;nbsp;&lt;i&gt;any&lt;/i&gt;&amp;nbsp;claim to be defended with what can&#39;t be checked.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- It forbids &quot;truth by assumption/circularity&quot;, because fabricators and liars can vouch for themselves - allowing&amp;nbsp;&lt;i&gt;any&lt;/i&gt;&amp;nbsp;system to authenticate itself.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- It forbids &quot;faith without (or against) reason&quot;, because devotion alone lacks the capacity to identify deception - allowing &lt;i&gt;any&lt;/i&gt;&amp;nbsp;belief to have equal &quot;confidence&quot;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- It forbids &quot;no rational distinction between mysteries and contradictions&quot;, because&amp;nbsp;falsehood can be protected by hiding behind ignorance or incomprehension.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- It forbids &quot;historical authority without traceability or resistance to fabrication&quot;, because then True revelation becomes indistinguishable from fabrication.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;Once these escape hatches are removed, what remains is not an arbitrary standard, but the &lt;i&gt;only&lt;/i&gt;&amp;nbsp;standard compatible with the question: &lt;b&gt;truth must be identified by correspondence with reality, coherence, non-circular justification, and historically constrained authority.&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;This standard is not uniquely &quot;religious&quot; - it&#39;s the same standard we use (whether implicitly or explicitly) for any field of study, whenever we genuinely care whether something is true.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;And under that standard, the conclusion naturally follows. We did not start by choosing a conclusion and hunting for support: we started with the meaning of the question itself -&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;to keep truth distinguishable from falsehood, at every level of the sieve, and without special pleading. I&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11px; background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;f we take the question seriously, then the True religion cannot be merely emotionally compelling; it must be distinguishable from fabrication in principle. It must be the worldview whose fundamentals align with reality, whose authority does not require epistemic blindness, and whose theology remains maximally coherent when compared with its alternatives. &lt;b&gt;The only remaining candidate, after applying all these filters, is Islam.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;As a result, the conclusion is&amp;nbsp;not merely that Islam is &quot;appealing&quot;, but that &lt;b&gt;Islam is the only remaining candidate that remains distinguishable from falsehood at every level of the sieve&lt;/b&gt; - from metaphysical fit with reality, to the nature of faith and contradiction, to the historical constraints of revelation, to the comparative coherence of its theological mechanism.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="420" width="810.14" x="20" y="9985" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <UserObject label="" link="data:page/id,dZVplhlVTvyQHVP8LEqG" id="Ms-guz4M4BKaG-NDeXWL-0">
          <mxCell connectable="0" parent="3-4-euxaZI7sU592ncQ1-1" style="group;rotation=-180;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="50" width="50" x="20" y="9920" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="Ms-guz4M4BKaG-NDeXWL-1" parent="Ms-guz4M4BKaG-NDeXWL-0" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;pointerEvents=0;align=center;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;fillColor=#E6E6E6;gradientColor=none;strokeColor=none;rotation=-360;opacity=1;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="50" width="50" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <UserObject label="" id="Ms-guz4M4BKaG-NDeXWL-2">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="Ms-guz4M4BKaG-NDeXWL-0" style="shape=flexArrow;endArrow=classic;html=1;rounded=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;fillColor=#B3B3B3;">
            <mxGeometry height="50" relative="1" width="50" as="geometry">
              <mxPoint x="50" y="25" as="sourcePoint" />
              <mxPoint x="10" y="25" as="targetPoint" />
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="WrumbxiehRIuW-RBPlB1-0" parent="3-4-euxaZI7sU592ncQ1-1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;pointerEvents=0;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;gradientColor=#b3b3b3;strokeColor=#666666;spacingTop=6;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;movable=1;resizable=1;rotatable=1;deletable=1;editable=1;locked=0;connectable=1;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;What&#39;s Next?&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 4px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;This project does not demand agreement, but it does put the ball in your court. You can now navigate topics that are often seen as overwhelming or inaccessible - topics that are necessary for having certain beliefs, but are normally hidden behind an air of complexity that makes it difficult to navigate for the average person. If you agree with the conclusion, now you know how these beliefs are grounded in reality. And if you reject the conclusion, you can now identify the precise disagreement - at which level - and what commitments that requires. This project gives you a map to navigate as you need:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;b&gt;1. Locate your exact point of resistance.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- If you feel unconvinced, identify the precise filter you reject. Then, identify clearly what your rejection commits you to: if you&#39;re unwilling to pay that epistemic price, then your resistance is not to the conclusion - it&#39;s to the implications of the method.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;b&gt;2. Test the sieve on yourself.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- Apply the filters to the beliefs you inherited and the beliefs you prefer. Remember that the question was never &quot;how do I critique others?&quot; but &quot;can I distinguish truth from falsehood - including in myself?&quot;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;b&gt;3. Separate &quot;mystery&quot; (what you don&#39;t comprehend or understand) from &quot;contradiction&quot; (what is not rational) in your own worldview.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- Ask: what is the difference between a metaphysical truth and a metaphysical falsehood?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- Answer: the one with a rational definition (and comes from a source you have reason to trust) is closer to truth than the one without a rational definition - which can only defend its coherence using speculation or ignorance.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;b&gt;4. Reflect on your definition of faith and the role of reason.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- Ask: do you use reason to establish the truth &lt;i&gt;before&lt;/i&gt;&amp;nbsp;placing faith, or does reason only apply &lt;i&gt;after&lt;/i&gt; faith has been established?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- Note: if the first, then that is what this project aims to demonstrate. If it is the second, then you deprive yourself of the mechanism necessary to identify false beliefs (as faith &lt;i&gt;can&lt;/i&gt;&amp;nbsp;be placed in falsehood). In that case, the only availble response to resolve valid doubt (in that falsehood) is to &quot;believe harder&quot;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;b&gt;5. Demand the same standard everywhere.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- If you require evidence and coherence in every serious domain of life, but suspend those standards only when theology is discussed, identify why.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- If your answer can be used to defend something you know to be false, or can be used by a liar to defend a fabrication, or aligns with any of the costs of disagreement, then that answer does not allow you to distinguish between truth and falsehood.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;b&gt;6. If you accept the sieve, follow it all the way.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- The project&#39;s goal is to make the identification of truth easy and accessible to anyone - but along the way, we made profound discoveries that directly impact our lives. If they are shown to be true, and you become aware of their truth, then apply those discoveries into your own life.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- Note that this project is not persuasively demanding, &quot;Islam is true, therefore become a Muslim&quot;. Rather, it is saying, &quot;Islam is the only candidate that remains distinguishable from falsehood at every level; here is the argument to verify for yourself.&quot; The rest is up to you.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;At the end of the day, the standard is simple: &lt;b&gt;a method that can justify both truth and falsehood cannot distinguish between them.&lt;/b&gt; The sieve was built to prevent that collapse, demystify apparent complexities, and allow anyone who disagrees to precisely identify what they reject and what commitments that earns them. If you accept that goal, the remaining work is straightforward: verify each filter for yourself -and then follow the conclusion wherever it leads.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="550" width="810.14" x="20" y="10420" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
